7.1 The SYSTEM PROVIDER shall undertake the following technical and operational obligations:
(a) Install, configure, and maintain cloud-synchronized Electronic Medical Record (EMR) workstations, digital radiology viewing consoles, and high-definition telemedicine diagnostic terminals at the City Health Office (CHO), Marilog District Hospital, Paquibato District Hospital, and Bunawan District Hospital within forty-five (45) calendar days from the execution of this Agreement;
(b) Provide twenty-four-hour technical helpdesk support, automated daily backups to redundant domestic servers, disaster recovery failover capability, and quarterly clinical software updates at no additional maintenance cost to the City Government;
(c) Conduct comprehensive hands-on training workshops for municipal physicians, public health nurses, midwives, pharmacists, and medical technologists on digital admission charting, ICD-10 diagnostic coding, electronic prescription workflows, and remote specialist consultation protocols; and
(d) Submit monthly system uptime reports, network latency audits, and anonymized epidemiological utilization summaries to the City Health Officer and the City Information Technology Center (CITC).

7.2 The LGU, through the City Health Office and the City Information Technology Center (CITC), shall undertake the following counterpart obligations:
(a) Designate two (2) permanent hospital information technology focal persons per participating facility to coordinate workstation installation, local area network routing, and role-based user authentication credentials;
(b) Provide uninterrupted electrical power, uninterruptible power supply (UPS) units, and dedicated fiber-optic internet connectivity at each hospital and district health site;
(c) Ensure that attending municipal medical personnel encode clinical admission notes, maternal delivery records, and PhilHealth electronic claim forms accurately within the platform; and
(d) Conduct semi-annual clinical quality assurance reviews to evaluate referral turnaround times for emergency obstetric, pediatric, and trauma cases originating from hinterland barangays.
